Modifications:

- retained the AppError translation-ID, immediate/default translation,
  wrapping, internal-detail, status, request-correlation, and bounded rendering
  concepts;
- integrated AppError with Proctor's RFC 9457 Problem Details boundary and
  separated translation parameters from explicitly public safe fields;
- retained Mattermost's 26-character z-base-32 UUID representation while using
  Go's crypto/rand directly and validating the canonical alphabet;
- retained the `PreSave`, `PreUpdate`, `IsValid`, and safe `Auditable`
  conventions while defining Proctor-specific institution and academic
  hierarchy models;
- separated user profiles from passwords and external identities instead of
  retaining Mattermost's combined user/authentication record;
- adapted team/channel membership validation into time-bounded academic-unit
  and class membership records without embedding authorization roles;
- adapted Mattermost roles into Proctor action permissions and added separate
  scoped role bindings;
- adapted sessions to omit raw tokens and role snapshots, with hashed
  access/refresh credentials and refresh-rotation lineage stored separately;
- adapted personal access tokens to require token hashes, mandatory expiry,
  explicit scopes, and optional academic-unit constraints;
- adapted purpose-specific user tokens to store hashes with explicit expiry and
  single-use consumption state;
- excluded Mattermost product-specific fields and validations.

The adapted files preserve Mattermost copyright notices where source was
directly adapted. Proctor-specific domain model files remain under the server's
AGPL license; their Mattermost-inspired conventions are recorded here.

