  Mattermost's MySQL, replicas, search replicas, licensing, and transparent
  store layers;
- retained embedded, locked Morph migrations but separated migration execution
  from ordinary server startup;
- adapted typed store errors while ensuring public error strings never include
  invalid values or driver details;
- adapted the per-model reusable store-conformance and thin SQL adapter-test
  pattern for every structural academic store;
- kept explicit SQL row representations, colocated with their corresponding
  `Sql<Model>Store`, instead of binding domain models directly to database
  column names;
- added Proctor-specific singleton-institution, generic academic hierarchy,
  hierarchy-cycle serialization, and same-parent-institution behavior;
- added PostgreSQL constraints for identity, enrollment, hashed credentials,
  and one active class per student and academic period.

