Modifications:

- retained stable action identifiers, named additive roles, current-state role
  resolution, deleted-role exclusion, per-model stores, batch role lookup,
  reusable store conformance, and deny-by-default behavior;
- replaced Mattermost's system/team/channel scopes with Proctor's
  institution, hierarchical academic-unit, and class scopes and made
  inheritance an explicit property of each recognized action;
- preserved syntactically valid unknown role permissions for
  upgrade/downgrade compatibility while refusing to authorize them until the
  closed action registry recognizes them;
- introduced separate time-bounded role bindings with transactionally
  serialized overlap checks and explicit validation of polymorphic scope
  references;
- adapted Mattermost's rich attempt/success/failure audit-record fields into
  authoritative PostgreSQL records instead of using its older minimal audit
  table or asynchronous audit-output queue;
- added immutable request-principal correlation, direct-peer metadata, stable
  node identity, resource and academic scope, bounded JSON prior/result state,
  attempt-only terminal transitions, and keyset pagination;
- made authorization-decision audit persistence fail closed and provided
  attempt-before-mutation primitives for future security-sensitive use cases;
- adapted Mattermost's reusable permission and user-visibility helpers around
  Proctor's immutable principal, current PostgreSQL role bindings, typed
  resources, default-deny cross-user policy, and separate audited resource and
  academic-scope fields;
- retained Mattermost's visible permission checks at privileged API handlers
  while keeping application use cases as independent authorization boundaries;
- added a Proctor-specific per-process sealed, request-bound, one-use
  authorization receipt so the application can verify and consume the exact
  audited API preflight decision without repeating role/resource queries;
- omitted Mattermost product, team, channel, scheme, license, enterprise,
  database-replica, and audit-output target assumptions.
- adopted Mattermost's per-domain `Init*` API ownership, central client-facing
  API URL suffix, `BaseRoutes` resource subrouters, named regex route
  variables, centrally populated request parameters, and typed handler
  wrappers while retaining Proctor's narrow composed application contract,
  immutable principal, duplicate-route detection, and Problem Details
  boundary;
- used Mattermost's first-user administrator behavior as a product reference
  but replaced its process-local first-user check with an explicit one-time
  PostgreSQL aggregate, durable installation marker, cluster-safe advisory
  lock, pristine-state validation, protected built-in role, and atomic success
  audit;
- adapted role administration around Proctor's scoped bindings and closed
  action registry, including immutable built-ins, institution-only
  system-administrator grants, and serialized last-administrator protection.

